tsrs-only: tsrs 0.20.0 narrowed the visibility of much of its API ("apply Hawk visibility fixes", oxc-project/tsrs#761:
`pub` items became `pub(crate)` or private). This restores `pub` on the items the Effect crates use, and only on
those: checker type fields (`IndexInfo`, `MappedType`, `ConditionalType`, `SubstitutionType`, ...), `Checker` fields
and methods the type parser and rules call, the change tracker's `NodeOptions` and methods, the code fix provider and
context fields, autoimport's `ExportID::export_name`, `Fix::type_only_alias_declaration`, `ModuleID::as_str` and
`ModuleID::as_file`, and a few others (see the diff). Each line keeps tsrs's code; only the visibility changes (and
rustfmt reflows the signatures that now fit on one line).

tsrs also moved its in-process LSP client (`lsptestutil`, the port of Go's testutil/lsptestutil) from tsrs_lsp's
library to its integration tests; crates/ets_fourslash drives it, so tsrs_lsp's library includes that file again as
the `lsptestutil` module.

tsrs 0.20.1 ("prepare 0.20.1", oxc-project/tsrs#823) narrowed more items and deleted unused ones. This widens the ones
the Effect crates use (`get_mapped_type_modifiers`, `is_private_identifier_symbol`, `ClassLikeBase::type_parameters`,
`change::new_tracker`, `create_diagnostic_for_node_in_source_file_or_compiler_diagnostic`, and the lsproto fields and
`Method::WORKSPACE_CONFIGURATION` the fourslash client sets), and restores, verbatim from tsrs 0.20.0, the deleted
`Checker::{get_error_type, resolve_external_module_symbol_exported, for_each_export_and_property_of_module}` and
`stringutil::lower_first_char`: Go exports them and the Effect crates call them, with no public tsrs equivalent.

